## #13 — rubric and translation parity (corpus work)

**Observed:** the entire Offertory · Lavabo · Orate fratres block
(Ordinarium Missæ) has a full Latin column and a **completely empty English
one** — Suscipe sancte Pater, Deus qui humanæ substantiæ, Offérimus tibi
Dómine, In spíritu humilitátis, Veni sanctificátor. The Lavabo psalm above it
and the Secreta below both have English. Blank, not wrong. Elsewhere Latin
rubrics appear with no English counterpart, and `! Gloria` renders **literally,
exclamation mark visible**, in both panes — raw corpus syntax reaching the
screen.

### ROOT CAUSE FOUND — the Ordinary gap is an ingest pairing bug, not a
### missing translation

`scripts/ingest-corpus.mjs:325-328` reads **both** `missa/Latin/Ordo/Ordo.txt`
and `missa/English/Ordo/Ordo.txt`, parses each with `parseOrdoFile` (`#`
headings), and pairs sections **by heading name**. Line 338:
`const er = e ? resolveLang(…) : { text: null, filled: false }` — no match means
English is written as `null`, which renders as the blank column.

But DO localises the headings themselves. Only **7 of 20** match:

| Latin | English |
|---|---|
| `# Offertorium` | `# Offertory` |
| `# Introitus` | `#Introit` |
| `# Credo` | `# Creed` |
| `# Graduale` | `# Gradual` |
| `# Lectio` | `# Lesson` |
| `#Oratio` | `# Collect` |
| `# Præfatio` | `# Preface` |
| `# Communio` | `# Communion` |
| `# Postcommunio` | `# Post Communion` |
| `# Conclusio` | `# Conclusion` |
| `# Incensatio` | `#Incense` |
| `# Preparatio Communionis` | `# Preparation for Communion` |
| `# Orationes Leonis XIII` | `# Leonine Prayers` |

Matching pairs: `# Incipit`, `# Kyrie`, `# Evangelium` ×3, `# Canon` — which is
exactly why Kyrie and Canon show English and the Offertory does not.

**Fix:** both files carry exactly 20 headings in the same order, so pair by
**ordinal index**, with a name map retained as a sanity assertion that the
ordinals have not drifted. This resolves all 13 sections at once. **No Route C
generation is needed for the Ordinary** — the English was in the vendored tree
the whole time. Requires a re-ingest to take effect.

### Remaining (genuinely missing) material

**Operator's triage, which matches the recorded policy in
`DOCS/MISSING-REFERENCES.md`:** no portion lacks *both* languages, so there is
always one side to work from.

- **Route S — scriptural.** Explicit or derivable citation → look up the
  counterpart from vendored PD sources (Clementine Vulgate for Latin,
  Douay-Rheims for English). Self-healing: because the corpus is a database and
  not a `.txt` tree, this re-resolves on every ingest.
- **Route A — DO-internal.** Text existing elsewhere in the vendored tree →
  substitute; supply in-style cross-translation where a language is missing.
- **Route C — Ordinary/euchology.** The Mass is not officially said in English,
  so no authoritative English is displaced; we author in-style under our own
  licence.

**Non-negotiable:** every supplied side is flagged `meta.translationSupplied`
(`'en'` = English is ours, `'la'` = Latin is ours) and rendered through the
`--supplied-ink` / `--supplied-bg` token pair with a provenance affordance.
Both the flag and the tokens are already specified in §3 of the register and
**neither is implemented**.

**Scale is the story.** 14,170 blocks are Latin-only. Route S absorbs a large
share automatically; what remains is genuine authored translation. At that
volume the English side becomes substantially *our* work rather than Divinum
Officium's — which is why the provenance boundary is the trust mechanism, not
bookkeeping, and why the About/licensing text will need to say so accurately.

**Tasks (to be numbered when folded into `CHECKLIST.md`):** regenerate the
census via the ingest v3 audit stage; implement `meta.translationSupplied` in
the ingest; implement the `--supplied-ink`/`--supplied-bg` rendering contract;
run Routes S/A/C; fix the `!` marker leaking into rendered output.

**Sequencing:** regenerates `assets/missal.db` (193 MB LFS). `BA.2R` already
owns "the single `assets/missal.db` re-ingest" for this wave — this rides with
it rather than triggering a second rebuild. Renovation-phase, not baseline.

